            <ArticleTitle>Thoracoscopic Surgery for a Congenital Bronchoesophageal Fistula With Pulmonary Sequestration in an Adult Woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-435</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1043-0679(17)30212-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.semtcvs.2017.07.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A congenital bronchoesophageal fistula with pulmonary sequestration is rare in adults. Here, we report the case of an adult woman having congenital bronchoesophageal fistula with intralobar pulmonary sequestration who successfully underwent thoracoscopic resection and showed a good postoperative course.</AbstractText>
